From ac0695a9199d447a97560ef0edc034f15ccd222e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michal Hrusecky <michal.hrusecky@nic.cz>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 15:55:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] kernel: add initial DVB support
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add kernel packages for DVB adapters, frontends and tuners. Not
everything is covered, but the list can grow over the time.

Userspace uses these through /dev/dvb, for example tvheadend from the
packages feed, which streams the tuners to network clients over HTTP
and HTSP.

Remote controller support (kmod-rc-core) goes into the Input modules
menu: rc-core depends only on INPUT and is not DVB specific.

Enabling DVB_CORE and RC_CORE makes parts of the media driver menu
visible which nothing in the tree has enabled so far, so kconfig has
no answer for them and stops for input. Add the 98 missing symbols to
the generic config. CONFIG_MEDIA_RC_SUPPORT, CONFIG_VIDEO_V4L2,
CONFIG_DVB_HD29L2, CONFIG_DVB_USB_FRIIO and CONFIG_IR_SIR do not exist
in kernel 6.18 anymore and are removed.

Tested on kernel 6.18.44, all 78 packages build with CONFIG_ALL_KMODS
and their module paths and kernel symbols were verified against the
kernel tree.

Signed-off-by: Michal Hrusecky <michal.hrusecky@nic.cz>
Signed-off-by: Karel Kočí <karel.koci@nic.cz>
Signed-off-by: Josef Schlehofer <pepe.schlehofer@gmail.com>
Link: https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/pull/24788
Signed-off-by: Robert Marko <robimarko@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit 1560c75fa250576b5d551a860d0928b2b1cee54a)
[Backport to 6.12: config-6.18 does not exist on openwrt-25.12, so
 answer the newly visible symbols in config-6.12. The 35 symbols were
 measured on vanilla 6.12.113 with 53 target configurations and the
 rest of the Turris series applied, where hack/0026 answers six more.]
Signed-off-by: Josef Schlehofer <pepe.schlehofer@gmail.com>
